# A `for` row whose key leaves (Semantics ch. 4, "`for`": a built block is kept "as long
# as its key is present"; ch. 9: a row "ends at the end of the tick its key leaves, having
# fired in that tick (R8)", and "a request fired by a place torn down in the same tick is
# still performed"; ch. 4, "`rebuild`": "its holds die with it ... each event of its own
# becomes `never`"). Each row asks the World on the block's `!ring` and gives its key on
# it; after the tick row 2 leaves, only row 1 asks and only row 1 is in the gathered
# event. Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.* | Test.*
test mod Tests

@rows: @unit
@rows:
    !drop <- Ui.Button($label=$"drop")                           # 0
    !ring <- Ui.Button($label=$"ring")                           # 1
    $names <- {{1: "one", 2: "two"}} then Remove $names, 2 on !drop
    !rang <- for k, $name <- $names:                            # 2/[k]
        Ui.Label($text=$name)                                     # 2/[k]/0
        Test.Log(!requests="ring {k}" on !ring)                  # 2/[k]/1
        @ k on !ring
    $heard <- 0 then $heard + (Len (Values !rang))
    Ui.Label($text=$"heard {$heard}")                             # 3
